<title>UK: UK wheat futures lower on currency driven market.</title>
<headline>UK wheat futures lower on currency driven market.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>LIFFE wheat futures finished a thin session slightly lower on Monday with currency dominating trade.</p>
<p>&quot;It's been all currency again, there no other interest,&quot; said a trader.</p>
<p>Wheat futures closed 0.50 to 0.10 stg down with most traded March finishing 0.15 stg down at 96.60 stg after trading 57 lots.</p>
<p>Total wheat turnover was 119 lots.</p>
<p>LIFFE barley futures were neglected.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8062</p>
</text>
